  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The primary driver of losses in Cycle #42 is severe fee drag (\u20b951.57 in fees vs \u20b9-24.09 net P&L, implying a positive gross P&L of \u20b927.48) coupled with a high 0.72% minimum stop-loss that resulted in outsized \u20b917\u2013\u20b924 losses on mid-morning reversals (specifically the 11:45 AM cluster on 2026-10-22). Additionally, trades with gross profits (Trade 4 on ICICIBANK and Trade 6 on TATASTEEL) flipped into net losses after transaction costs due to an overly ambitious 1.4% target that failed to materialize before mean reversion or EOD square-off. Late afternoon entries (after 13:45) also suffered from decaying intraday momentum and time-decay into the close.",
    "learning": "In small-capital NSE cash equity intraday trading, high target thresholds (1.4%) cause winning excursions to round-trip into breakeven stops or sluggish EOD exits where statutory fees flip positive gross alpha into net losses; compressing profit targets to capture high-probability impulsive bursts while tightening initial stop-loss bounds and demanding higher sweep volume confirmation maximizes net expectancy after brokerage and STT.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.15,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.85,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 0.9,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #42 Quantitative Review & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing in Cycle #42 revealed that the strategy generated positive gross alpha (+\u20b927.48) but was dragged into a net deficit (\u20b9-24.09) by \u20b951.57 in execution fees and oversized stop-outs during mid-session liquidity sweeps (notably the Oct 22 11:45 IST synchronized reversal across ITC, ICICIBANK, and TATASTEEL). To convert gross edge into net profitability, we are compressing `min_target_pct` from 1.40% to 1.15% to harvest intraday momentum before afternoon stagnation sets in, and lowering `breakeven_trigger_r` from 1.05R to 0.90R to lock in fee-adjusted buffers earlier. Simultaneously, we are tightening `min_sl_pct` from 0.72% to 0.55% to cap downside tail risk on false breakouts while raising `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` from 2.65x to 2.85x to filter out low-conviction mid-day volume spikes."
